   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ אֵין מְפַנִּין מִבַּיִת לְבַיִת, אֲבָל מְפַנֶּה הוּא לַחֲצֵרוֹ. אֵין מְבִיאִין כֵּלִים מִבֵּית הָאוּמָּן, אִם חוֹשֵׁשׁ לָהֶם — מְפַנָּן לְחָצֵר אַחֶרֶת.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «One may not move» his possessions «from house to house» during the intermediate days of a Festival, «but he may move» them «to his courtyard» if that is necessary. «One may not bring» home «utensils from the house of a craftsman» after he has completed his work, but «if one is concerned about them» that if he leaves them in the craftsman’s house they are likely to be stolen, «he may move them to another courtyard.»"
  }
